00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Legally Blonde is a 2001 American comedy film directed by Robert Luketic
and written by Karen McCullah Lutz and Kirsten Smith.

15
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Based on Amanda Brown's novel, it stars Reese Witherspoon, Luke Wilson, Selma
Blair, Matthew Davis, Victor Garber, and Jennifer Coolidge.

16
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
The story follows Elle Woods (Witherspoon), a sorority girl who attempts to win back her ex-boyfriend Warner Huntington III (Davis) by getting a Juris
Doctor degree at Harvard Law School, and in the process, overcomes stereotypes against blondes and triumphs as a successful lawyer.

17
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
The outline of Legally Blonde originated from Brown's experiences as a blonde going to Stanford Law School while being obsessed
with fashion and beauty, reading Elle  magazine, and frequently clashing with the personalities of her peers.

18
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
In 2000, Brown met producer Marc Platt, who helped her
develop her manuscript into a novel.

19
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
Platt brought in screenwriters McCullah Lutz and Smith
to adapt the book into a motion picture.

20
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
The project caught the attention of Luketic, an
Australian director new to Hollywood.

21
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film was released on July 13, 2001, and was a hit with audiences, grossing $142 million worldwide on an $18 million budget,
as well as receiving positive reviews from critics, with praise for Witherspoon's performance in particular.

22
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
It was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best
Motion Picture: Musical or Comedy.

23
01:18:51,428 --> 01:18:57,428
Witherspoon received a Golden Globe nomination for Best Actress – Motion Picture
Musical or Comedy, and the 2002 MTV Movie Award for Best Female Performance.

24
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
A sequel, Legally Blonde 2: Red, White & Blonde, was released in 2003, while
another sequel was announced to be in development in 2018.

25
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Legally Blonde also spawned a media franchise with various adaptations, including a stage musical, which premiered on Broadway in 2007, a direct-to-video spin-off, Legally
Blondes, released in 2009, and an upcoming prequel television series about Woods's high school years, Elle, scheduled to premiere in 2026 on Amazon Prime Video.

26
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
The film explores themes of father murder, blonde,
superficiality, beauty salon, law school.

27
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
